.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_ADD_DATA 3 2026-08-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_add_data \- add an in-memory file to an MPQ archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_add_data("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "mpq_archive,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        const uint8_t *" "buffer,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t " "size,"
.BI "        const mpq_file_options_s *" "options"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds \fIsize\fP bytes from caller-owned \fIbuffer\fP under \fIfilename\fP.
The call begins, writes, and finishes one member using the same file options
as the streaming writer. NULL \fIoptions\fP selects writer defaults; the
buffer need only remain valid until this call returns.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP after the member is staged in the writer
archive, or a negative libmpq error. Archive publication still requires
\fBlibmpq__archive_close\fP().
.SH ERRORS
Invalid writer state or storage options return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP;
duplicate names return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP; invalid or excessive
sizes return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP. Allocation, compression, and I/O
errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_add_path (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_write (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_timestamp (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_finish (3)
